  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A significant storm system impacted the United States during the Thanksgiving holiday, causing widespread power outages and travel disruptions along the East Coast. At the peak of the weather event, nearly 900,000 customers lost power, and hundreds of flights were cancelled. By Friday, November 27, utility companies had restored service to approximately 420,000 customers, leaving roughly 480,000 still awaiting electricity. The severe conditions necessitated the postponement of the annual Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade in New York City, which had previously been placed under an emergency declaration. The rescheduling has created complex logistical and financial hurdles for participating groups, including various marching bands. While cleanup operations proceed in affected regions, the nation continues to navigate the aftermath of the storm as individuals prepare for the remainder of the holiday weekend.",
